---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---
<Site
  title="About · Ouijit"
  description="Ouijit is built by one person, Prentice Bjerkeseth. Free, open source under AGPL, no account and no telemetry, and the plan is to keep it that way.">
  <main class="compare-content about-content">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Ouijit is a desktop app for running coding agents in parallel, each in its own git worktree. It is free,
      open source under AGPL-3.0, and made by one person.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no account and no telemetry. The only usage figure that exists is the download count on GitHub.
      If Ouijit ever charges for anything, it will be a feature with its own running cost, such as hosted
      environments or sync. The app stays free.
    </p>
    <p>
      I started it for the fun of building with AI and switched to it for all my work within a week. It runs
      agents as the CLIs they are, in real terminals, because that is where their capability arrives first. A
      chat interface will come on top of that, not in place of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Many tools like this are taking venture money, being acquired, or closing. I intend to keep this one
      independent.
    </p>
    <p class="about-sign"><a href="https://github.com/pbjer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Prentice Bjerkeseth</a></p>
  </main>
</Site>
